# Temp
.tmp/

# Claude Code (settings.json is tracked; everything else is local/runtime).
# Use `.claude/*`, not `.claude/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so the `!` line below is dead against a bare `.claude/`.
# But a mid-pattern slash anchors to this directory, so `.claude/*` covers only
# the root one where bare `.claude/` covered every depth; `*/**/.claude/`
# restores that. Nested .claude dirs hold settings.local.json, which carries
# machine-local MCP config and absolute-path allow rules — never commit it.
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
*/**/.claude/

